# Granot Extension Architecture

- WXT browser extension for Chrome MV3 and Firefox MV2. Use WXT/browser globals (`webextension-polyfill` style) and validate with `pnpm compile`, `pnpm build`, and `pnpm build:firefox` before shipping.
- `src/config.ts` owns Granot URL patterns, `VANTAGE_API_BASE`, and bundled `VITE_VANTAGE_API_SECRET`; Vantage `/api/v1` calls send the secret as `x-api-secret`.

## Layer Map

- `src/entrypoints/*` are thin runtime adapters: content script reads Granot, background schedules automation, popup bootstraps UI.
- `src/parsers/granot/*` are pure DOM parsers for Follow Up Estimates, current form-lead edit pages, and call/booked lead tables. Keep Granot DOM knowledge here.
- `src/workflows/{form-leads,call-leads}/*` contains UI-free preview, payload, sync, and cycle logic reused by popup actions and background automation.
- `src/api/*` is the Vantage HTTP boundary; `src/utils/api.ts` only re-exports legacy imports.
- `src/messaging/tabs.ts` is the shared tab/frame transport. It resolves active or pinned tabs and aggregates `PARSE_*`/`DUMP_TABLES` responses across all frames.
- `src/app/state.ts` is shared type vocabulary only. Runtime state initialization lives in `src/entrypoints/popup/app/state.ts`.
- `src/auto-sync/*` owns unattended background automation: settings, lock, cycle summaries, persisted cycle history, and the runner.
- `src/entrypoints/popup/{app,ui,workspaces}` owns the popup shell, typed DOM lookup, rendering, event wiring, and workspace actions.

## Entrypoints

- `src/entrypoints/granot-crm.content.ts` declares `allFrames: true` because Granot uses framesets/iframes. It handles `PING`, `DUMP_TABLES`, `PARSE_FOLLOW_UP_ROWS`, `PARSE_CURRENT_FORM_LEAD`, and `PARSE_CALL_LEAD_TABLES`. It must remain read-only: never mutate the CRM page or add controls.
- `src/entrypoints/background.ts` reconciles the `granot-sync:auto-sync` alarm from stored settings and calls `runBackgroundAutoSync()` on alarm fire.
- `src/entrypoints/popup/main.ts` only resolves popup/detached mode, builds `AppContext`, loads persisted preferences, attaches events, renders, and starts initial workspace loads.

## Popup Structure

- `app/context.ts`, `state.ts`, `router.ts`, `persistence.ts`, `events.ts`, `render.ts`, `shell.ts`, and `auto-sync.ts` form the popup shell.
- `ui/dom.ts`, `status.ts`, and `components.ts` provide typed DOM handles and shared format/status helpers.
- Each workspace uses `workspaces/<name>/actions.ts` for async scan/sync/storage/API work and `render.ts` for DOM output.
- Workspace ids in code are `form-leads`, `form-edit-lead`, `call-leads`, `automation`, `diagnose`, and `debug`.
- Popup persistence key `granot-sync:popup-state-v1` stores active workspace plus list interval/filter preferences only; never persist scan results.

## Feature Model

- Form Leads scans the visible `Follow Up Estimates` section only. `ref_no` is the Mongo `_id` for Vantage `FormLead`; `prior` maps to Vantage `quoted`.
- Only exact `prior` values are syncable: `0 -> quoted=false`, `1 -> quoted=true`. Unsupported values are shown and skipped by default.
- Form-lead sync preflights `GET /api/v1/form-leads/:id`, compares current `quoted`, and PATCHes only when the value changes. PATCH triggers server-side WaitUntil Google Sheet sync.
- Current Lead sync parses the active Granot edit page, previews the parsed lead, and can apply a quoted override from the `form-edit-lead` workspace.
- Call Leads parses follow-up and booked sections for enrichment/reconciliation preview. Booked reconciliation writes only when the explicit workflow setting enables it.
- Manual scan-and-sync loops run from `popup/app/auto-sync.ts` while the popup is open.
- Unattended scan-and-sync runs through `background.ts` -> `auto-sync/background-runner.ts`; defaults are disabled, preview-only, Form Leads enabled, call workflows disabled, and fallback form matches disabled.
- Detached popup mode is handled by `app/shell.ts` using `?detached=1&targetTabId=...` to keep a popup window tied to a Granot tab.
- Diagnostics and Debug workspaces use `PING` and `DUMP_TABLES` to troubleshoot content-script injection and parser visibility.

## Automation Storage

- `granot-sync:auto-sync-settings-v1`: normalized background settings.
- `granot-sync:auto-sync-cycles-v1`: newest-first background cycle log, capped to 25 cycles per workflow.
- `granot-sync:auto-sync-lock-v1`: 5-minute stale-lock mutex preventing overlapping background cycles.

## Editing Rules

- Keep entrypoints thin; put new behavior in parsers, workflows, API modules, or workspace `actions.ts`/`render.ts`.
- Never import popup UI/state modules from `src/entrypoints/background.ts` or `src/auto-sync/background-runner.ts`.
- Use `src/messaging/tabs.ts` for all content-script calls from popup or background code.
- Preserve row-level outcomes in UI/cycles: updated, unchanged, skipped/unsupported, invalid id, not found, and failed.
- Do not sync Booked Jobs as Form Leads or use CSV links as source of truth unless the task explicitly changes that contract.

## Browser Loading Notes

- Prod load folders: `.output/chrome-mv3/` from `pnpm build`, `.output/firefox-mv2/` from `pnpm build:firefox`.
- Dev folders: `.output/chrome-mv3-dev/` from `pnpm dev`, `.output/firefox-mv2-dev/` from `pnpm dev:firefox`.
- Chrome MV3 dev content-script registration depends on the running `pnpm dev` WebSocket; if it stops, Scan/Debug may return zero frame responses.
- After rebuilding or reloading the extension, hard-reload the Granot tab so the content script reinjects. If scans return zero, check for the content-script startup log in the Granot tab and confirm the expected Follow Up Estimates or Booked Jobs section is visible.
